\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Open, Lord, my inward ear,
\par And bid my heart rejoice;
\par Bid my quiet spirit hear
\par Thy comfortable voice;
\par Never in the whirlwind found,
\par Or where earthquakes rock the place,
\par Still and silent is the sound,
\par The whisper of Thy grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. From the world of sin, and noise,
\par And hurry I withdraw;
\par For the small and inward voice
\par I wait with humble awe;
\par Silent am I now and still,
\par Dare not in Thy presence move;
\par To my waiting soul reveal
\par The secret of Thy love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thou didst undertake for me,
\par For me to death wast sold;
\par Wisdom in a mystery
\par Of bleeding love unfold;
\par Teach the lesson of Thy Cross,
\par Let me die with Thee to reign;
\par All things let me count but loss,
\par So I may Thee regain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Show me, as my soul can bear,
\par The depth of inbred sin;
\par All the unbelief declare,
\par The pride that lurks within;
\par Take me, whom Thyself hast bought,
\par Bring into captivity
\par Every high aspiring thought
\par That would not stoop to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lord, my time is in Thy hand,
\par My soul to Thee convert;
\par Thou canst make me understand,
\par Though I am slow of heart;
\par Thine in whom I live and move,
\par Thine the work, the praise is Thine;
\par Thou art wisdom, power, and love,
\par And all Thou art is mine.
\par                                Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
